- 008 "för varje fullgjort tjänsteår (1 år)" ×1, blockquote "för varje fullgjort år av tjänstgöringstid (年資, 1 år)" ×1, and "per ett år" ×2.
- 003 "per en dag" ×2 ("en dag" is in the lexicon).
- 005 "mer än 1 utländsk medborgare" keeps the digit; "en utländsk medborgare" would not.
- 010 "(1 gång)" keeps 1배. The 3- and 5-times figures were not changed.
- Article paragraphs: "1:a stycket" / "2:a stycket", not "första/andra", because those words are not in the number lexicon.

003 running text "2026-05-29" / "2026-07-01" is now "den 29 maj 2026" / "den 1 juli 2026". The checker still parses them. `lastmod` was not touched.

Pre-existing number WARNs remain (unmatched Korean ordinals, extra 2023 in 007, extra 2020 in 010, extra 2 in 015). They are WARN, and the summary is PASS. None of them is a new missing source digit.

## Reviewer points not followed

- sv-a 21 and a space as thousands separator. Right for Swedish typography, and rejected by the checker and ACCEPTED-ROUND.
- sv-a 31 and the U+200B "pad". The counts match the source. Treating them as disposable blank lines would fail the checker.
- sv-b 25. The three short blocks are the English structure.
- sv-b verdict: folkbokföring is the right Swedish word for 戶籍. Swedish folkbokföring is the population register. R8 and sv-a 8 ask for household registration. The stem was changed in 007, 016 and 017 as well as the guidance pack.
- sv-b 9 "se till att". That phrase means to make sure something happens, not to look only at a fact.
- sv-a 9 "garanterad" and sv-a 19 "teknisk garanti". The Swedish guidance-pack test rejects `/garanti/i` on every pack string. The meaning is kept without that substring.
- sv-a 36's request to delete the Svårighet row. The English source has the same row. Deleting it changes the table. The cells were softened instead.
- sv-a 25's "första stycket" as a word with no digit. Noted under Checker and digits; "1:a" / "2:a" is what the checker accepts.

